*  GIT.IGNORES(IGL) — the account's ignore patterns, both lists, as one @AM list.
*  Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE).
*
*  TWO NAMESPACES AND BOTH COUNT.  The account's own bulk list is what
*  `GIT IGNORE` writes; `.gitignore` is what a developer reaches for first and
*  what a repository shared with plain git already has.  `status` read both and
*  `add` read neither, so this is the loader they now share (mv_git#133).
*
*  Read through GIT.OSFILE rather than OSREAD directly: OSREAD is UniData-only,
*  and this has to work on UniVerse too.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.IGNORES(IGL)
      AM = CHAR(254) ; LF = CHAR(10)
      IGL = ""
*  NOT COMPILED ON MVX, the same split BP/GIT.MASTER makes: there `add` and
*  `status` are the ENGINE, which applies libgit2's own gitignore rules and
*  needs nothing from here.  The body would not compile there anyway -- MVX has
*  no `CONVERT ... IN` -- and a standalone subroutine is compiled on EVERY
*  platform whether or not anything calls it, which is what makes that matter.
$IFNDEF MVX
      CALL GIT.OSFILE("READ", @PATH : "/GITIGNORE", IGL, IGOK)
      IF NOT(IGOK) THEN IGL = ""
      CONVERT LF TO AM IN IGL
      IGL2 = ""
      CALL GIT.OSFILE("READ", @PATH : "/.gitignore", IGL2, IG2OK)
      IF IG2OK AND IGL2 # "" THEN
         CONVERT LF TO AM IN IGL2
         IF IGL = "" THEN IGL = IGL2 ELSE IGL := AM : IGL2
      END
$ENDIF
      RETURN
      END
